{"agent_id":"pp3g-i81g-produce-the-design-sketch-for-the-154-durable-a1fc","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:09:20.518600813Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4f679348-c35f-4ba0-ab80-900788e81b19","comment_uuid":"0e2ddc5e-77b8-47cb-9b99-8318f0699435","author":"pp3g-i81g-produce-the-design-sketch-for-the-154-durable-a1fc","content":"Plan: (1) reconcile fork naming — verified sst/opencode is an HTTP 301 redirect to anomalyco/opencode (same repo, renamed); canonical upstream = anomalyco/opencode, tag v1.18.11/v1.18.12 both exist and provider.ts is byte-identical between them. (2) exact patch = one-line wrapSSE guard removal (confirmed against canonical source). (3) non-SSE deadline: recommend distinct longer body-completion deadline (preserves hy3 F2). (4) error surfacing + retry budget: root cause located — SessionRetry.policy is an UNBOUNDED schedule (Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata, no recurs cap) and ResponseStreamError maps to isRetryable:true in message-v2.ts fromError; Effect.logError('stream error') exists in llm.ts but session retry status never halts. (5) rebuild/replace/rollback via bun build + atomic mv. (6) verification harness reuse + new slow-non-SSE test. CRITICAL FINDING: installed opencode was upgraded 1.18.11→1.18.12 at 2026-08-04 03:15:59, wiping the #145 binary patch (guard re-present at offset 97992552, if(false) marker gone) — the durable fix is needed NOW, not hypothetically.","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:09:20.512840054Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:h+ZBNM6xwANC5bCBGspFTRRgx5tPdw6CRHcWH9R7WBs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg22VA8Vi6EEevLSrJx0oOCtIzgRpaGvIfOtg+AR9m394AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAorSDvAPzfkJk8j7MzQhSGVpvFEFFoC1ViR4XBvSuHJf2+bX0ogcqnJozA6AXK0641K7B7uNkuIjwCPsUz3LODQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:h+ZBNM6xwANC5bCBGspFTRRgx5tPdw6CRHcWH9R7WBs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg22VA8Vi6EEevLSrJx0oOCtIzgRpaGvIfOtg+AR9m394AAA