{"agent_id":"pp3g-i81g-produce-the-design-sketch-for-the-154-durable-a1fc","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:18:16.862404947Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4f679348-c35f-4ba0-ab80-900788e81b19","comment_uuid":"c6b37375-4407-4c25-8b8d-c143b6652110","author":"pp3g-i81g-produce-the-design-sketch-for-the-154-durable-a1fc","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=design drafted (361-line doc, all 6 sections: fork naming resolved, exact patch, non-SSE deadline decision, retry budget location, rebuild/rollback, verification matrix incl. 2 new tests) next=post final design as result comment blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:18:16.855059235Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:h+ZBNM6xwANC5bCBGspFTRRgx5tPdw6CRHcWH9R7WBs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg22VA8Vi6EEevLSrJx0oOCtIzgRpaGvIfOtg+AR9m394AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAlkb5CVeup0L3Lg1knOHu5CcnygdlB1myuDfWrq9OOHYxdtPwHZndr87remhGrhJ3QS6wciE3qK5Ujlt2NwjIBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:h+ZBNM6xwANC5bCBGspFTRRgx5tPdw6CRHcWH9R7WBs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg22VA8Vi6EEevLSrJx0oOCtIzgRpaGvIfOtg+AR9m394AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM/WaakapGJ+3DClOoHcCasOOfkUV+Vac0zhCAJ6mXT2UPLzYGHxGFCXKLhnvgMzjtuHBV7xXHMg+RNZbDKUxwg="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-i81g-produce-the-design-sketch-for-the-154-durable-a1fc","agent_seq":9,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:18:43.910966676Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4f679348-c35f-4ba0-ab80-900788e81b19","comment_uuid":"6070f165-b325-4371-9051-efae52aa2dec","author":"pp3g-i81g-produce-the-design-sketch-for-the-154-durable-a1fc","content":"# DESIGN: Durable opencode silent-hang fix (#154) — design sketch\n\n**Sub-issue**: #175 · **Parent**: #154 · **Epic**: #156\n**Designer**: Builder pp3g-i81g (design-only task; no code or binary changes made)\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\n\n---\n\n## 0. Current-state finding (verified this session — changes the urgency)\n\n**The installed opencode was upgraded `1.18.11 → 1.18.12` at `2026-08-04 03:15:59`, silently wiping the #145 emergency binary patch.** Verified in the live binary:\n\n- Installed: `/home/claude-code/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.3/lib/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe` reports `opencode --version` = `1.18.12`, size `179,349,632` bytes, mtime `2026-08-04 03:15:59`.\n- The #145 marker `if(false)return` appears **0 times**; the original guard `if(!$.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\"))return $;` is back at offset `97992552`.\n- `sst/opencode` resolves via GitHub 301 redirect to `anomalyco/opencode`; tags `v1.18.11` and `v1.18.12` both exist; `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` is **byte-identical** between the two tags (2011 lines, `rtk diff` = identical).\n\n**Consequence**: the silent-hang bug described in #144 is LIVE again as of this morning's upgrade. The durable fix is not hypothetical — it is the only protection until an upstream PR (#39516 / #35743) lands. This design is the durable replacement for the wiped interim patch.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Fork strategy\n\n### 1.1 Naming reconciliation (sst/opencode vs anomalyco/opencode)\n\n**Verdict: `sst/opencode` and `anomalyco/opencode` are the SAME repository — the repo was renamed; GitHub serves a 301 redirect from the old name.**\n\nEvidence (verified this session):\n- `gh api repos/sst/opencode` returns `full_name: \"anomalyco/opencode\"`.\n- `curl -sI https://github.com/sst/opencode` → `HTTP/2 301` → `location: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode`.\n- `gh api repos/anomalyco/opencode/tags` lists both `v1.18.11` and `v1.18.12`; release `v1.18.11` published `2026-08-01`.\n- The #145 claim \"binary matches sst/opencode @ v1.18.11\" is consistent: the tag `v1.18.11` on the canonical repo matches the embedded source (the extracted `provider.ts.orig` is byte-identical to the canonical v1.18.11 file).\n- The #145 upstream comments correctly went to `anomalyco/opencode` (issue #26487, PR #39516) — that is the canonical, current name.\n\n**Canonical upstream**: `anomalyco/opencode` (formerly `sst/opencode`; the old name is a redirect and should not be used for new clones/remotes).\n\n### 1.2 Fork + pin\n\n- **Create a fork of `anomalyco/opencode`** (project-owned; e.g. under the same org as this repo).\n- **Pin the fork at tag `v1.18.12`** — the version currently installed and the npm package version (`opencode-ai@1.18.12`), so `opencode --version` stays coherent with the managed package. NOTE: issue text says \"v1.18.11\" (correct when written); `provider.ts` is byte-identical between v1.18.11 and v1.18.12, so the same one-line patch applies verbatim to either tag. Pinning v1.18.12 avoids a version-skew (npm says 1.18.12, binary reports 1.18.11).\n- **Track the patch as a committed divergence on the fork** (one commit: `fix(provider): apply body-read deadline to all responses`), keeping a clean rebase path against upstream tags. Same pattern as the crosslink fork documented in `.crosslink/knowledge/crosslink-fork.md`.\n\n### 1.3 How the fix survives opencode upgrades\n\nThe upgrade vector: `opencode upgrade` / `npm install -g opencode-ai@latest` replaces the npm-managed `bin/opencode.exe` (verified: today's 1.18.12 upgrade did exactly this, wiping the patch). Survival design (layered):\n\n1. **Primary — launch-chain indirection.** Install the fork-built binary at a durable, npm-independent path, e.g. `~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe`, and change the `REAL` variable in the `~/.local/bin/opencode` wrapper to point at it. The launch chain (`crosslink kickoff → tmux → claude wrapper → opencode`) uses the wrapper, so future `opencode upgrade` / npm updates of the stock package rewrite only the npm-managed binary and **cannot** touch the fork binary. The wrapper's models-cache rewrite runs against the fork binary unchanged.\n2. **Secondary — disable self-update.** Set `\"autoupdate\": false` in the global config (`~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`) so the built-in updater (`packages/opencode/src/cli/upgrade.ts`: `if (config.autoupdate === false || Flag.OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE) return`) never silently replaces the binary. Optionally set `OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=1`.\n3. **Tertiary — documented re-apply procedure.** `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md` (mirrors `crosslink-fork.md`) records: canonical upstream identity, pinned tag, patch, build steps, and the invariant \"any deliberate upgrade = rebuild fork at new tag, re-apply patch, re-run install steps\". See §5.4.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Exact patch (source-level diff)\n\nFile: `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` (canonical @ v1.18.12; identical @ v1.18.11). Two hunks.\n\n### Hunk 1 — `wrapSSE` region (lines 37–82): keep SSE per-chunk wrapper; ADD a non-SSE total-completion wrapper\n\n**Replace the guard-only removal with a dispatcher + `wrapBody` (design requirement 3).**\n\n```diff\n const OPENAI_HEADER_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT = 300_000\n+const DEFAULT_BODY_TIMEOUT = 1_800_000 // 30 min, non-SSE body-completion deadline\n \n function wrapSSE(res: Response, ms: number, ctl: AbortController) {\n   if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || ms <= 0) return res\n   if (!res.body) return res\n-  if (!res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")) return res\n \n   const reader = res.body.getReader()\n   const body = new ReadableStream<Uint8Array>({\n     async pull(ctrl) {\n       const part = await new Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof reader.read>>>((resolve, reject) => {\n         const id = setTimeout(() => {\n           const err = new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"SSE read timed out\")\n           ctl.abort(err)\n           void reader.cancel(err)\n           reject(err)\n         }, ms)\n \n         reader.read().then(\n           (part) => {\n             clearTimeout(id)\n             resolve(part)\n           },\n           (err) => {\n             clearTimeout(id)\n             reject(err)\n           },\n         )\n       })\n \n       if (part.done) {\n         ctrl.close()\n         return\n       }\n \n       ctrl.enqueue(part.value)\n     },\n     async cancel(reason) {\n       ctl.abort(reason)\n       await reader.cancel(reason)\n     },\n   })\n \n   return new Response(body, {\n     headers: new Headers(res.headers),\n     status: res.status,\n     statusText: res.statusText,\n   })\n }\n+\n+// NEW: total body-completion deadline for non-SSE responses.\n+// The deadline is a single timer for the WHOLE body: it fires only if the body\n+// does not complete within `ms`, never on slow-but-progressing chunks.\n+// This preserves the original guard's intent (do not abort slow-but-legitimate\n+// non-streaming bodies, hy3 F2) while still killing a body that never closes.\n+function wrapBody(res: Response, ms: number, ctl: AbortController) {\n+  if (typeof ms !== \"number\" || ms <= 0) return res\n+  if (!res.body) return res\n+  const reader = res.body.getReader()\n+  const body = new ReadableStream<Uint8Array>({\n+    async start(ctrl) {\n+      const id = setTimeout(() => {\n+        const err = new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"Body read timed out\")\n+        ctl.abort(err)\n+        void reader.cancel(err)\n+        ctrl.error(err)\n+      }, ms)\n+      try {\n+        for (;;) {\n+          const { done, value } = await reader.read()\n+          if (done) {\n+            clearTimeout(id)\n+            ctrl.close()\n+            return\n+          }\n+          ctrl.enqueue(value)\n+        }\n+      } catch (e) {\n+        clearTimeout(id)\n+        ctrl.error(e instanceof Error ? e : new Error(String(e)))\n+      }\n+    },\n+    async cancel(reason) {\n+      ctl.abort(reason)\n+      await reader.cancel(reason)\n+    },\n+  })\n+  return new Response(body, {\n+    headers: new Headers(res.headers),\n+    status: res.status,\n+    statusText: res.statusText,\n+  })\n+}\n```\n\n### Hunk 2 — `resolveSDK` fetch wrapper (lines ~1736–1767): dispatch on content-type\n\n```diff\n         const customFetch = options[\"fetch\"]\n         const chunkTimeout = options[\"chunkTimeout\"]\n         const headerTimeout = options[\"headerTimeout\"]\n+        const bodyTimeout = options[\"bodyTimeout\"] ?? DEFAULT_BODY_TIMEOUT\n         delete options[\"chunkTimeout\"]\n         delete options[\"headerTimeout\"]\n+        delete options[\"bodyTimeout\"]\n \n         options[\"fetch\"] = async (input: any, init?: BunFetchRequestInit) => {\n           const fetchFn = customFetch ?? fetch\n           const opts = init ?? {}\n           const chunkAbortCtl = typeof chunkTimeout === \"number\" && chunkTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n+          const bodyAbortCtl = typeof bodyTimeout === \"number\" && bodyTimeout > 0 ? new AbortController() : undefined\n           const headerTimeoutMs = headerTimeout === false ? undefined : headerTimeout\n           const headerTimeoutCtl = typeof headerTimeoutMs === \"number\" ? timeoutController(headerTimeoutMs) : undefined\n           const signals: AbortSignal[] = []\n \n           if (opts.signal) signals.push(opts.signal)\n           if (chunkAbortCtl) signals.push(chunkAbortCtl.signal)\n+          if (bodyAbortCtl) signals.push(bodyAbortCtl.signal)\n           if (headerTimeoutCtl) signals.push(headerTimeoutCtl.signal)\n           if (options[\"timeout\"] !== undefined && options[\"timeout\"] !== null && options[\"timeout\"] !== false)\n             signals.push(AbortSignal.timeout(options[\"timeout\"]))\n \n           const combined = signals.length === 0 ? null : signals.length === 1 ? signals[0] : AbortSignal.any(signals)\n           if (combined) opts.signal = combined\n \n           const res = await fetchFn(input, {\n             ...opts,\n             // @ts-ignore see here: https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/16682\n             timeout: false,\n           }).finally(() => headerTimeoutCtl?.clear())\n \n-          if (!chunkAbortCtl) return res\n-          return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+          const isSSE = res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")\n+          if (isSSE) {\n+            if (!chunkAbortCtl) return res\n+            return wrapSSE(res, chunkTimeout, chunkAbortCtl)\n+          }\n+          if (!bodyAbortCtl) return res\n+          return wrapBody(res, bodyTimeout, bodyAbortCtl)\n         }\n```\n\n**Note on the emergency fallback**: the #145 one-liner (delete the guard line only, so `chunkTimeout` wraps all bodies) is the *minimal* variant of this same patch. The design's recommended durable form is the dispatcher above, which is strictly safer (see §3). The fork should carry the dispatcher; the one-liner exists in git history for emergency re-use.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Non-SSE deadline design — decision + rationale\n\n**Decision: OPTION B — add a distinct, longer body-completion deadline for non-SSE responses. Do NOT relax the guard to apply `chunkTimeout` (per-chunk idle timeout) to all bodies.**\n\n| | Option A: relax guard entirely | Option B (RECOMMENDED): distinct body-completion deadline |\n|---|---|---|\n| Non-SSE hang (application/json never closes) | killed after chunkTimeout | killed after bodyTimeout (longer, still bounded) |\n| Slow-but-legitimate non-SSE body (hy3 F2) | **false-aborted** when any inter-chunk gap > chunkTimeout | **preserved** — only a body that NEVER completes is aborted |\n| Semantics | per-chunk idle timeout applied to non-streaming bodies (semantically wrong) | total body-completion deadline (semantically correct for non-SSE) |\n| Regression risk (luna #150 / hy3 #153 F2) | HIGH (untested slow-non-SSE regression) | LOW (original intent retained) |\n| Changes to SSE path | none | none |\n| Code | one-line deletion | ~30 lines (dispatcher + wrapBody), reviewed below |\n\n**Rationale** (converges with the 4-reviewer consensus #150–#153 and the #154 requirements):\n1. hy3 F2 is the specific failure the reviewers flagged: a legitimate non-SSE body with a gap > `chunkTimeout` between chunks would be aborted under Option A. With `chunkTimeout=300000` in prod this is unlikely for typical JSON, but it is a real behavioral regression vs. the original design intent and is untested by the #145 verification table.\n2. The non-SSE failure mode is a body that never completes — a *total-completion* deadline is the precise guard for that. A per-chunk idle timeout is the right guard for SSE (streams must keep producing), not for a single-shot body.\n3. `wrapBody` starts ONE timer and clears it only on `done`; it cannot false-fire on a slow-but-steady body. This directly implements \"preserve original intent of not aborting slow-but-legitimate non-streaming bodies\" (#154 requirement 2).\n4. Config surface: new provider option `bodyTimeout` (default `DEFAULT_BODY_TIMEOUT`, recommended `1_800_000` = 30 min — generous for legit slow bodies, well under the 1h outer `timeout`, so the body deadline fires first with a descriptive error instead of a generic overall timeout). `chunkTimeout` semantics for SSE are unchanged.\n5. `headerTimeout` behavior untouched (no-headers case still surfaces 4 visible `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError` entries, per #144 row 3).\n\n**Explicit trade-off**: non-SSE bodies that legitimately take > 30 min to fully deliver would now be aborted (they were never bounded before). This is acceptable and configurable via `bodyTimeout`; it is the price of killing the 10.9h hang signature.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Error surfacing + retry budget — where and how\n\n### 4.1 Root cause (verified in v1.18.12 source)\n\n- The chunkTimeout abort rejects with `ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(\"SSE read timed out\")` (`provider.ts` wrapSSE; wrapBody will do the same with \"Body read timed out\").\n- `MessageV2.fromError` (`packages/opencode/src/session/message-v2.ts` ~line 626) maps `ResponseStreamError` → `APIError { isRetryable: true }`.\n- `SessionRetry.retryable()` (`packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts`) returns a retry payload for any retryable APIError.\n- `SessionRetry.policy()` uses **`Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata` — an UNBOUNDED schedule** (no `Schedule.recurs`, no max-attempt cap). Every failure that `retryable()` deems retryable schedules another attempt forever.\n- `SessionProcessor.process` (`packages/opencode/src/session/processor.ts` ~line 660) wraps the LLM stream in `Effect.retry(SessionRetry.policy({...}))` → the silent infinite retry loop with exponential backoff (observed gaps ~3.5/5/7/11/19/33s in #144).\n- The **visible ERROR path already exists but is unreachable today**: when `Effect.retry` eventually gives up, `Effect.catch(halt)` runs `halt()` (~line 600) which does `Effect.logError(\"process\", ...)` + publishes `Session.Event.Error` + sets `assistantMessage.error` + status idle. Because the schedule never gives up, zero ERROR entries ever appear.\n\n### 4.2 Design\n\n1. **Cap the retry schedule** in `packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts`:\n   - Add `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (recommended default **3**: initial + 2 retries; configurable via provider option `retry.maxAttempts` or env).\n   - In `policy()`'s step, return `Cause.done(meta.attempt)` when `meta.attempt > RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` — the identical stop mechanism `retryable()` already uses for non-retryable errors.\n2. **Visible retryable ERROR entry**: with the cap, the chunkTimeout/bodyTimeout abort now flows: abort → `ResponseStreamError` → `APIError{isRetryable:true}` → 2 retries with backoff → schedule gives up → `halt()` → `Effect.logError` ERROR entry + `Session.Event.Error` + message error + status idle. The agent loop sees a real error and the flag stops lying as RUNNING.\n3. **Retry budget**: 3 attempts total (≈ initial + 2× backoff ≈ 2s+4s = ~6s of retry before terminal error in the no-headers case; with `retry-after` headers the budget still caps the number of attempts, not the delay). This bounds the previously infinite loop while keeping resilience for genuinely transient provider hiccups.\n4. **Distinct timeout messages** (\"SSE read timed out\" vs \"Body read timed out\") so logs distinguish the path; both carry `metadata.code = ProviderResponseStreamError` via the existing `MessageV2.fromError` mapping.\n5. **Relationship to #146**: with ERROR surfacing + budget, the #135/#146 watcher kill/restart remains the outer safety net for *other* failure modes; it is no longer the only recovery for this one.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Rebuild / replace / rollback\n\n### 5.1 Build (bun)\n\nPrereq: `bun` is **not installed** on this machine (verified). Steps (from `VERIFICATION.md` + upstream `script/build.ts`):\n\n```bash\n# 1. install bun\ncurl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash   # adds ~/.bun/bin\n\n# 2. clone the fork (canonical upstream, pinned tag)\ngit clone https://github.com/<org>/opencode-fork.git\ncd opencode-fork && git checkout v1.18.12\n\n# 3. apply the fork patch (Hunks 1+2 from §2, saved as .patch in the fork repo)\ngit apply opencode-145-durable.patch\n\n# 4. install + build (single-target = current platform)\ncd packages/opencode\nbun install\nbun run build --single        # script/build.ts: builds dist/opencode-linux-x64/bin/opencode\n\n# 5. smoke test\n./dist/opencode-linux-x64/bin/opencode --version   # expect 1.18.12\n```\n\nNote: build.ts embeds the web UI (`app` build) and generates `modelsData`; a full fork build takes several minutes and needs network for npm deps. `--single` restricts to the current OS/arch to avoid building all 12 targets.\n\n### 5.2 Replace (atomic, with backup retained)\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup\n\n# backup current stock binary (the wiped 1.18.12) and the #145 artifacts\ncp /home/claude-code/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.3/lib/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe \\\n   ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup/opencode.exe.stock-1.18.12\n# (historical: /tmp/opencode-145-patch/opencode-patched.exe = 1.18.11 patched; opencode.exe.ORIGINAL = 1.18.11 stock)\n\n# atomic same-filesystem rename into the durable path\nmv ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup/opencode.exe.previous   # if exists\ncp packages/opencode/dist/opencode-linux-x64/bin/opencode ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe\nchmod +x ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe\n\n# point the wrapper at the fork binary\n# edit ~/.local/bin/opencode: REAL=\"<fork path>\" (currently the nvm symlink)\nREAL=\"$HOME/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe\"\n\n# disable self-update\n# edit ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json: add \"autoupdate\": false\n```\n\nVerification after replace: `opencode --version` = 1.18.12; `opencode models` works (wrapper cache rewrite path).\n\n### 5.3 Rollback\n\n```bash\n# restore the stock binary to the fork path (or flip wrapper REAL back to the nvm symlink)\ncp ~/.local/opencode-fork/backup/opencode.exe.stock-1.18.12 ~/.local/opencode-fork/bin/opencode.exe\n# or: sed -i 's#REAL=.*#REAL=\"<nvm symlink>\"#' ~/.local/bin/opencode\nopencode --version   # confirm 1.18.12 stock\n```\n\nRollback criterion: if any provider regresses (e.g. legitimate non-SSE bodies aborting), restore stock and report to the operator; the #146 watcher remains the safety net meanwhile.\n\n### 5.4 Documentation location (upgrade survival)\n\n- **`.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md`** — the canonical fork-divergence page (mirrors `.crosslink/knowledge/crosslink-fork.md`): upstream identity (`anomalyco/opencode`, formerly `sst/opencode`), pinned tag v1.18.12, the §2 patch, build/replace/rollback commands, autoupdate-disable note, and the invariant \"any upgrade = rebuild from the fork at the new tag and re-apply the patch\".\n- Optional pointer in `ORIENTATION.md` / `AGENTS.md` tooling notes.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification harness\n\n### 6.1 Reuse\n\n- Fake hanging server: `/tmp/opencode-hang-test/server.js` (HANG_MODE 0 = no response at all → headerTimeout case; 1 = headers then hang → chunkTimeout case; 2 = one SSE chunk then hang; CONTENT_TYPE env: text/event-stream | application/json).\n- Harness config: `/tmp/opencode-hang-test/cfg/opencode.json` — `chunkTimeout: 3000`, `headerTimeout: 2000`, `timeout: 15000` (plus NEW `bodyTimeout` for non-SSE tests).\n- Command: `opencode run --model hangtest/hang-model \"Say hi.\"` with `HOME`/config pointed at the harness cfg.\n- Artifacts retained in `/tmp/opencode-145-patch/` (patched binary, ORIGINAL, VERIFICATION.md, per-mode logs).\n\n### 6.2 Test matrix (patched fork binary)\n\n| # | Scenario | Expected result | Proves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | application/json + hang (mode 1, ct=application/json) | abort within `bodyTimeout`; ≤3 attempts total; **visible ERROR** entry + Session.Event.Error; process exits with error, not EXIT 124 | non-SSE hang killed; retry budget; error surfacing |\n| 2 | text/event-stream + hang (mode 1, ct=text/event-stream) | abort within `chunkTimeout` (unchanged); ≤3 attempts; visible ERROR | SSE path unchanged; budget |\n| 3 | no response at all (mode 0) | headerTimeout fires; 4 visible `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError` entries (unchanged) | headerTimeout untouched |\n| 4 | healthy application/json (complete body) | normal completion, EXIT 0, no retries | no regression on fast non-SSE |\n| 5 | healthy text/event-stream (mode 2) | \"Hello world\", EXIT 0, no retries | no regression on SSE |\n| 6 | **NEW: slow-but-legitimate non-SSE body** (application/json, server writes chunks with inter-chunk gaps > chunkTimeout but total < bodyTimeout) | **completes normally, EXIT 0, no abort** | hy3 F2 preserved — the reason for Option B |\n| 7 | **NEW: ctl.abort() per-request** (two concurrent requests to the same server: one hangs/aborts, the other healthy) | healthy request completes unaffected | hy3 F4 — abort is per-request, not shared (source also confirms: `new AbortController()` per fetch call inside the wrapper, line 1745) |\n| 8 | chunkTimeout/bodyTimeout sensitivity (2000 vs 4000) | retry cadence tracks the configured value | mechanism is the config knob |\n\n### 6.3 Slow-non-SSE server (new harness mode)\n\nAdd `HANG_MODE=3` (or a `SLOW_CHUNK_MS` env) to `server.js`: sends `application/json` headers + first chunk, then writes remaining chunks with a delay per chunk (e.g. chunk every 2s for 6 chunks with `chunkTimeout=3000`/`bodyTimeout=30000`). Test 6 must pass (completes) and test 1 with the same server minus the completion (never finishes) must abort within `bodyTimeout`.\n\n### 6.4 Retry-budget verification\n\nAssert the server log shows **exactly ≤3 POSTs** for hang scenarios (initial + ≤2 retries), then an ERROR entry and a non-zero/error exit — vs the current unbounded loop (7+ POSTs and climbing, EXIT 124 only from the outer kill).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Open items / handoff\n\n- Implementer: build the fork @ v1.18.12, apply §2 patch, wire `RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS` in `retry.ts`, run §6 matrix, install per §5.2, write `.crosslink/knowledge/opencode-fork.md`.\n- Reviewer: assess against §6 matrix and the 4-reviewer consensus.\n- Upstream tracking: PR #39516 (chunkTimeout for every streamed body) and PR #35743 (eventstream matching) remain the proper long-term fixes; our fork is the pinned divergence until they land (same pattern as crosslink fork).\n- Immediate operational note: because the 1.18.12 upgrade wiped the patch, the **stock binary is currently vulnerable** — the fork install should be treated as high-priority.","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:18:43.905118390Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:h+ZBNM6xwANC5bCBGspFTRRgx5tPdw6CRHcWH9R7WBs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg22VA8Vi6EEevLSrJx0oOCtIzgRpaGvIfOtg+AR9m394AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAXjgKlMIOW7rJH7fd7lEuPKTctQsok9rcTSkvXvxsx/DEaQXGNA9faH5wp1kqGm6A6M9wCsYw2t5guDYowGHcBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:h+ZBNM6xwANC5bCBGspFTRRgx5tPdw6CRHcWH9R7WBs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg22VA8Vi6EEevLSrJx0oOCtIzgRpaGvIfOtg+AR9m394AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBjBcb6RLN/Ow3cidzdrGxPceuAgaXDcp3v+bYPVpupF0zFFW6biXxMgU/JAgbgI63OEhHWaQNfF4YXVg6Mvlgg="}
